      "text": "To solve the given problem, we start by letting \\( y = \\frac{4x - 16}{3x - 4} \\). The equation then becomes:\n\n\\[\ny^2 + y = 12\n\\]\n\nThis is a quadratic equation in terms of \\( y \\). We can rewrite it as:\n\n\\[\ny^2 + y - 12 = 0\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula. The quadratic formula states that if \\( ay^2 + by + c = 0 \\), then \\( y = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\). Here, \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = 1 \\), and \\( c = -12 \\). Substituting these values into the quadratic formula gives:\n\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-12)}}{2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1 + 48}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm 7}{2}\n\\]\n\nThis results in two solutions for \\( y \\):\n\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-1 + 7}{2} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad y = \\frac{-1 - 7}{2} = \\frac{-8}{2} = -4\n\\]\n\nSo, we have two possible values for \\( \\frac{4x - 16}{3x - 4} \\), which we will simplify to find \\( y \\):\n\n1. For \\( y = 3 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4x - 16}{3x - 4} = 3 \\implies 4x - 16 = 3(3x - 4) \\implies 4x - 16 = 9x - 12 \\implies -16 + 12 = 9x - 4x \\implies -4 = 5x \\implies x = -\\frac{4}{5}\n\\]\n\n2. For \\( y = -4 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4x - 16}{3x - 4} = -4 \\implies 4x - 16 = -4(3x - 4) \\implies 4x - 16 = -12x + 16 \\implies -16 + 16 = -12x - 4x \\implies 0 = -16x \\implies x = 0\n\\]\n\nWe now need to check which value of \\( x \\) makes the original expression defined. For \\( y = 3 \\), \\( (3x - 4) \\neq 0 \\) and \\( (4x - 16) \\neq 0 \\), so \\( x \\neq -\\frac{4}{5} \\neq \\frac{16}{4} = 4 \\). Thus, \\( x = -\\frac{4}{5} \\) does not satisfy both conditions. For \\( y = -4 \\), \\( (3x - 4) \\neq 0 \\neq (4x - 16) \\), so \\( x = 0 \\) does not ensure the denominator is not zero, and it is not a valid solution either. Thus, we discard both and simplify checking the discriminants.\n\nWe also note for \\( x = \\boxed{-4} \\).",
