      "text": "Let $y=\\dfrac{4x-16}{3x-4}.$  Then $y^2+y-12=0,$ so $y=-4$ or $y=3.$\n\nIf $y=-4,$ then $\\dfrac{4x-16}{3x-4}= -4,$ which always gives an integer value for $x.$  So $x\\geq \\boxed{8}$.\n\nIf $y=3,$ then $\\dfrac{4x-16}{3x-4}= 3,$ which gives $\\frac{x}{x-1}= 5,$ and the solution to this equation $= \\boxed{\\frac{5}{4}}.$\n\nAs the largest value of $x,$ $x=\\boxed{\\frac{5}{4}}$ is the correct answer. The answer is \\frac{5}{4}",
